    {
      "name": "create_checkout_link",
      "description": "Open a Stripe checkout session for one edition and return its payment link. Give that link to the buyer: they enter their card on Stripe's own page, and the ebook is emailed to them once the payment clears. The link expires after 24 hours, and nothing is charged until the buyer pays. For a paperback, no direct link is returned — print orders need a shipping address, so the buyer is sent to the product page instead. The returned price is always in euros (currency is EUR); if another currency was requested, Stripe converts it on its payment page and the amount charged there differs from price — checkout_currency names that currency, so do not announce price in it. Pass the item_id returned by list_editions whenever you have one.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
